From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:13:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath9k: pass the NAPI context to mac80211

Now that RX runs from a NAPI poll, use ieee80211_rx_napi() so that
mac80211 hands data frames to napi_gro_receive() instead of
netif_receive_skb_list(), and the stack can merge TCP segments before
they are routed, bridged or delivered locally.

ath_flushrecv() also calls ath_rx_tasklet(), from process context while
the hardware is being stopped, so it keeps passing no NAPI context.

Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c
index 7855274..c060e3a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c
@@ -1252,7 +1252,8 @@ int ath_rx_tasklet(struct ath_softc *sc, int flush, bool hp, int budget)
 		if (ieee80211_is_ack(hdr->frame_control))
 			ath_dynack_sample_ack_ts(sc->sc_ah, skb, rs.rs_tstamp);
 
-		ieee80211_rx(hw, skb);
+		/* ath_flushrecv() runs outside the NAPI poll */
+		ieee80211_rx_napi(hw, NULL, skb, flush ? NULL : &sc->napi);
 
 requeue_drop_frag:
 		if (sc->rx.frag) {
